sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch06-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch06-20: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.87" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.872"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/proof" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Additivity implies a binomial self-similarity identity, which is a proof that every additive rule emulates itself and produces nested patterns. Among the 256 elementary rules the linear ones can be listed exhaustively, and the claim that rules 90 and 150 are the only distinct cases is a finite check under stated symmetries. Rule 184's three-cell emulation is another finite identity. The word rare is the only soft residue." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Test all 256 elementary rules for linearity over GF(2), reduce the linear ones by color swap and reflection, and check the claimed block emulations for rules 90, 150, and 184. An extra linear equivalence class, or a failed emulation identity, would refute the corresponding clause." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Fundamentally different means up to the usual color and reflection symmetries.", "Rare, outside the elementary linear list, is a sample remark attached to a sharp classification." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch06-20 by Grok 4.7: 0.88" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch06-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch06-20--grok--operationalizability> .
